1. A scan fills the cache with long segments
file_segments_by_size_eq_count=1	bytes_by_segment_size_eq_downloaded_size=1
has_bytes=1
2. Point reads
file_segments_by_size_eq_count=1	bytes_by_segment_size_eq_downloaded_size=1
3. Dropping the cache removes everything
segments=0	bytes=0
4. A scan larger than the cache evicts file segments; the counters stay consistent
file_segments_by_size_eq_count=1	bytes_by_segment_size_eq_downloaded_size=1
5. The asynchronous metrics have one key per bucket
metric=FilesystemCacheBytesBySegmentSize	keys=['1048576','16777216','2097152','4194304','524288','8388608','inf']
metric=FilesystemCacheFileSegmentsBySize	keys=['1048576','16777216','2097152','4194304','524288','8388608','inf']
6. The asynchronous metrics count file segments and bytes
segments_include_this_cache=1	segments_not_above_files=1	bytes_include_this_cache=1	bytes_not_above_cache_bytes=1
